    /* The extra top padding is load-bearing — it keeps the first line of text
       clear of the specular catch-light, which is the one bright spot on the
       panel and the only place contrast could suffer. */
    padY: 34,
    padX: 30,
    /* LAGOON. Greener and a little lighter than the old 12,51,60, which went
       muddy grey over turquoise footage. This sits in the same hue family as
       the water, so the panel reads as a patch of DEEPER water rather than as
       a foreign dark rectangle. Picked on the real footage in the preview's
       tint lab, not from a swatch. */
    rgb: "6, 52, 54",
    /* Alpha at the TOP of the panel — its thinnest, lightest point. The CSS
       gradient carries it to x1.42 at the bottom by itself.

       The curve is deliberately SHALLOW (0.46 -> 0.56, not 0.36 -> 0.56):
       0.56 was approved on the real footage with the thickness held constant,
       so keeping the start close to it means what ships matches what was
       signed off. The small remaining rise still spares the dark opening
       frames, which genuinely need less protection.
       See the CONTRAST note in the stylesheet: 0.52 is the floor here.       */
    desktop: { dark: 0.46, mid: 0.51, bright: 0.56 },
    /* Mobile stays thicker: the copy sits directly over the products with no
       open water to move into. NOT yet reviewed on a real phone. */
    mobile:  { dark: 0.54, mid: 0.60, bright: 0.66 },
    /* How much of the soft halo to keep behind the panel. Pulled back from
